  "scientific_interpretation": [
    "Blind C4R hydrological fidelity plus C4S full common-cohort authority supports a resolved shared-host cost-fidelity signal for LARE R3-R8 on this fixed-water-table B01 workload.",
    "The result is purpose-frontier evidence, not a claim that every low-dimensional LARE member is hydrologically adequate for a real application.",
    "R4 is the blind minimum dimension that crossed R2 and FMC on the groundwater fidelity vector in C4R, while R12 was required to cross FMC when mapped 10-cm profile fidelity was included.",
    "C4T timing shows LARE R3-R8 resolved cheaper than fine R16 on this host; LARE R12 is resolved more expensive than R16.",
    "Same-partition CoRichards can be much more hydrologically faithful at higher dimension but is resolved more expensive than R16 on this workload because the complete admitted fallback policy is included.",
    "FMC is also resolved more expensive than R16 in this compiled C4T screen; this does not supersede separately governed F-ROMV2 D25 evidence because workload, implementation path and timing experiment differ.",
    "Without independently sourced application thresholds, frontier membership alone cannot choose R3, R4, R5, R6 or R8 for a real groundwater application.",
    "The next scientific requirement is a purpose-dependent application acceptance envelope, beginning with groundwater use, not another closure or timing optimization."
  ],
